# Git author/committer map for the public repository.
#
# The commit metadata in this repository's history was written with
# personal email addresses. Publishing the repository would publish that
# metadata, and GitHub permanently links every commit to its author
# address. A history rewrite replaces it.
#
# Format: <original> <replacement>
#
# The replacement address is the project's public one. `dev@functionfly.com`
# is a role address, not a person's inbox.
#
# `MicroHD <<personal address — see .mailmap>>` and
# `functionflycom <<personal address — see .mailmap>>` are personal Gmail
# addresses; `MicroHD <<personal address — see .mailmap>>` is a personal address at
# another organisation. All three are mapped to the role address.
#
# Applied by:
#   git filter-repo --mailmap .mailmap

MicroHD <<personal address — see .mailmap>> FunctionFly Dev <dev@functionfly.com>
MicroHD <<personal address — see .mailmap>>        FunctionFly Dev <dev@functionfly.com>
functionflycom <<personal address — see .mailmap>> FunctionFly Dev <dev@functionfly.com>
